# Security

- Read `SECURITY.md` before changing anything here.
- Tenancy: every query on customer data is filtered by `org_id` from the authenticated principal, never from the request body. Reviewers reach only the task they hold. A new endpoint gets a test that another org gets 404 (not 403, no existence leak) on its resources.
- Roles: check the role in the route dependency (`api/deps.py`), not in the web app only. Platform-admin routes stay under `/v1/admin`.
- Money paths (quotes, invoices, ledger, reviewer pay, payouts): `Decimal` only, idempotency keys on creates, ledger entries balance to the cent, no update or delete of posted entries.
- Provenance and ledger are append-only; never add a code path that updates or deletes those rows.
- Webhooks: HMAC SHA-256 with timestamp, constant-time compare, retries with backoff, auto-disable on repeated failure. Never send secrets in payloads.
- File parsing: XML with entity resolution and network access off; size and count limits on uploads; never execute or render uploaded content.
- Web: the API token stays in the httpOnly cookie and goes through `src/app/api/proxy` (D-036). Nothing secret in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Secrets live in env files that git ignores and in server env in the cloud. Never in code, logs, commits, evidence files or chat output. New settings go into `.env.example` as `ARBITER_<FIELD>` with an empty or dev-only value and a comment on where the value comes from.
- Never paste a token into a shell command; the shell guard blocks it.
- Hand changes here to the `security-reviewer` subagent before the gate.
